  data:  # fb33
    kind: work_item  # fb33
    title: "smart-test exits 1 on fully-green runs (all tests pass + all changed source at 100%): false-red + scoped-coverage verdict absent from captured (non-tty) output"  # fb33
    status: todo_hard  # fb33
    priority: 3  # fb33
    parent:  # fb33
    tags:  # fb33
    - dogfood  # fb33
    - tooling  # fb33
    - test_infra  # fb33
    isbefore: []  # fb33
    duplicate_of: []  # fb33
    not_duplicate_of: []  # fb33
    pr_ref:  # fb33
    description: "smart-test (scripts/smart-test, the `pytest` shim per ADR-0010) exits 1 on a\nFULLY GREEN run, producing a false-red indistinguishable from a real failure\nwithout manual forensics.\n\nObserved (two runs this session, WI-lirub and WI-sapaj branches):\n- pytest result: 16333 passed, 5 skipped, 4 xfailed, 0 failed, 0 errors\n  (ground truth from .ci/pytest-output.log, ANSI-stripped).\n- All changed source files at 100% coverage (verified via\n  `coverage report --data-file=.coverage` on the 10 baseline-drifted files —\n  every one at 100%).\n- Yet the wrapper's overall exit status is 1.\n\nTwo compounding problems:\n1. FALSE EXIT CODE. Candidate cause: the exit-code re-derivation in run_pytest\n   (scripts/smart-test ~line 404-410) uses `grep -qE \"[0-9]+ passed\" && ! grep -q\n   \"failed\"` to reset exit_code to 0 — but `grep -q \"failed\"` MATCHES \"xfailed\",\n   so whenever the run has any xfailed tests (there are always 4), the reset to 0\n   is skipped and a non-zero exit_code survives. (Note: PIPESTATUS after\n   `pytest ... || true` should already be 0, so the true root cause may be\n   elsewhere — the scoped-coverage check at ~line 938-964, gated on \"tests\n   passed\", or the pytest-shim/background-capture path. Needs a focused repro.)\n2. MISSING GREEN SIGNAL IN CAPTURED OUTPUT. When smart-test is run with stdout\n   redirected to a file (non-tty, e.g. background job), the summarize section and\n   the scoped-coverage verdict (\"✅ All changed source files are at 100%\n   coverage\", ~line 964) are ABSENT from the captured log — it jumps from\n   \"Running tests...\" + one divider straight to the end. So even the\n   handoff-recommended signal (\"All changed source files at 100%\") isn't\n   visible, forcing manual `coverage report` forensics to confirm green.\n\nImpact: every local smart-test run this session reported exit=1 despite being\ngreen, costing ~15-30 min of investigation per occurrence to distinguish from a\nreal failure. CI is unaffected (uses its own baseline + full coverage). This is a\ndev-loop reliability issue, not a correctness issue in the tool under test.\n\nRepro: `BASE_BRANCH=selfh/dev pytest > /tmp/st.log 2>&1; echo $?` on a branch with\na green, 100%-covered change → prints 1; `.ci/pytest-output.log` shows 0 failed.\n\nscripts/smart-test is NOT a governance file, so this is fixable without human\napproval. Fix direction: (a) make the \"failed\" grep word-boundary-safe so\n\"xfailed\" doesn't match (e.g. `grep -qE \"[0-9]+ failed\"`); (b) ensure the scoped\nverdict prints to the captured log; (c) add a focused test reproducing a green +\n100% run and asserting exit 0.\n\nDiscovered while landing WI-lirub / WI-sapaj."  # fb33
    fields: {}  # fb33
- op: discuss  # d5dd
  at: '2026-07-11T22:36:42Z'  # d5dd
  by: agent  # d5dd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d5dd
  clock: 2  # d5dd
  nonce: d5dd  # d5dd
  message: "COMBINED DESIGN — smart-test false-red root cause + coverage-enforcement architecture fix (investigation 2026-07-11, dev @ 8dc4100e5f).\n\nNOTE: this supersedes the item's original problem-#1 \"xfailed grep\" prime suspect, which is REFUTED below. The xfailed grep is a real LATENT bug but is NOT the cause of the observed exit=1.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n1. ROOT CAUSE (evidence-backed)\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n1a. The `xfailed` grep theory is REFUTED as the cause of exit=1.\n  - run_pytest (smart-test:401-419) does `pytest … > LOG 2>&1 || true; exit_code=${PIPESTATUS[0]}`.\n    Empirically, PIPESTATUS[0] after `cmd || true` is ALWAYS 0 (the `true` runs last on failure;\n    short-circuits on success).\n  - On a green-with-xfailed log, branch 3 (`grep -qE \"[0-9]+ passed\" && ! grep -q \"failed\"`) IS\n    skipped because \"xfailed\" matches \"failed\" — BUT the fallthrough leaves exit_code at the\n    PIPESTATUS default of 0. So run_pytest returns 0 on green. Verified by isolating the exact\n    conditional against a synthetic \"16333 passed … 4 xfailed\" log.\n  - Conclusion: the xfailed grep is a masked latent bug (fix defensively), not the false-red.\n\n1b. The false-red comes from the scoped coverage gate (smart-test:956-962; the ci.yml twins at 911/1156).\n  coverage.py 7.13.3 behavior, measured directly:\n    • include a file with data @100%             -> exit 0\n    • include a 100% file + a no-data file        -> exit 0 (no-data file silently omitted)\n    • include ONLY no-data file(s)                -> exit 1  (\"No data to report.\")\n    • include a <100% file                        -> exit 2  (fail-under)\n  Ground truth from the last real green run (baseline 038d4c4a; 12 changed source files; 459 test\n  files / 16338 passed / 0 failed): replaying the gate's exact command against that run's on-disk\n  .coverage -> exit 0 (all 12 changed files at 100%, TOTAL 100%). So the false-red is\n  DATA-DEPENDENT, not deterministic: it fires only when the affected-test SLICE under-covers >=1\n  changed source file. Demonstrated on current-tree data: 12-clean-files + cfg.py (60% under this\n  slice) -> exit 2.\n\n1c. The real root is an ADR COMPOSITION GAP.\n  - ADR-0010 makes the affected-test slice deliberately fast-but-INCOMPLETE (the lazy full-suite is\n    \"the final gate\"; the slice is stable-hypergumbo reverse-deps; subprocess tests contribute no\n    coverage).\n  - ADR-0011 Part 2 step 5 enforces 100% coverage on EVERY changed source file — validated (its\n    Example Output) only on a file whose full coverage happens to live inside its affected tests.\n  - Enforcing a total-coverage invariant against a deliberately-incomplete test slice is the defect.\n    It stays invisible until the changed set contains a file whose 100% depends on tests OUTSIDE its\n    reverse-dep closure (integration-covered / parametrized-cross-cutting / subprocess-covered).\n  - What makes it routine now: the last-green-sha marker (the coverage baseline) is 50 commits / 2\n    days stale (038d4c4a, 2026-07-09), inflating \"changed source files\" with ~50 commits of\n    already-merged work whose full test sets the slice does not all select.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n2. VERIFIED COVERAGE-ENFORCEMENT TOPOLOGY (2026-07-11)\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  Gate            | When            | Coverage scope     | Hard-fails <100%?\n  ci.yml (per-PR) | every PR        | changed files only | YES (scoped, --include+--fail-under=100)\n  smart-test      | local dev loop  | changed files only | YES (scoped)\n  full-suite.yml  | 01:00/13:00 UTC | whole codebase     | NO — pytest runs carry NO --cov-fail-under;\n                  |                 |                    |   coverage is scraped only for the badge/\n                  |                 |                    |   marker; aggregate verdict keys on TEST\n                  |                 |                    |   RESULTS, not coverage\n  nightly.yml     | 05:30 UTC       | whole codebase     | YES (--cov-fail-under=100)\n  release.yml     | on tag          | whole codebase     | YES\n\n  Consequence: the BLOCKING path (per-PR ci.yml + full-suite, which drives stop-the-line) guarantees\n  100% only on CHANGED files. Whole-codebase coverage currently rests entirely on nightly (daily;\n  and its propagation under failover is unverified). full-suite — the job that drives stop-the-line —\n  has zero coverage teeth today.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n3. STALE-MARKER VERDICT (de-risking full-suite teeth): NOT coverage debt.\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  All 6 marker-required packages are at 100% whole-codebase coverage in isolation, measured LOCALLY\n  2026-07-11 (this is exactly the marker's write condition):\n    core / mainstream / common / extended / tracker  -> check-package-coverage --serial, exit 0\n    rust-analyzer                                     -> direct pytest, 101 passed, 194/194 stmts,\n                                                         \"Required test coverage of 100% reached\"\n  So the marker's coverage condition IS satisfied at HEAD. The 50-commit staleness is a WRITE-PATH /\n  FAILOVER artifact, not debt:\n    - full-suite.yml writes the marker via `git push origin badges --force` (line 1043) and POSTs the\n      aggregate status to a HARDCODED codeberg.org endpoint (line 1052).\n    - Under CI failover (codeberg down — confirmed: `ci-debug runs` -> HTTP 000; origin/badges 253\n      commits stale) those codeberg-targeted writes silently no-op (`|| echo \"Push failed…\"`).\n    - selfh/badges last advanced to 038d4c4a on 07-09 and hasn't since — attributable to the codeberg\n      write breakage and/or a flaky full-suite job tripping `conclusion != success` (line 977 gates\n      the marker-write step, so any job flake silently skips it).\n  Exact per-run cause not pinned (the `runs` API is down; full-suite is schedule-attached, not on\n  HEAD). But the decisive point for teeth is settled: adding --cov-fail-under would NOT immediately\n  stop-the-line for coverage — there is nothing below 100%.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n4. DESIGN — sequenced fix\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nSTEP 1 — smart-test correctness (self-contained; immediate dev-loop win; PR \"A\")\n  1a. De-conflate baselines. Enforce 100% coverage on BRANCH-OWN changes:\n      diff(merge-base(HEAD, <authoritative-dev>)..HEAD) ∪ staged ∪ unstaged — NOT the distant-marker\n      diff. Branch-own files are guaranteed to be in the affected slice (the branch's own tests are\n      selected); already-merged drift files were gated at their own merge. Write branch-own\n      CHANGED_SOURCE_FILES into .ci/affected-tests.txt so ci.yml's scoped check stays consistent.\n      IMPORTANT: this removes the current (unreliable, false-red-drowned) per-PR \"drift enforcement\".\n      The RELIABLE whole-codebase catch is restored by STEP 3 (teeth) — so the cross-cutting\n      \"not-my-problem\" coverage crack is CLOSED by step 3, not left open. Steps 1a and 3 are a pair.\n  1b. xfailed grep: `! grep -q \"failed\"` -> `! grep -qE \"[0-9]+ failed\"` (defensive; latent today).\n  1c. Treat coverage.py exit 1 (\"No data to report\") as NOT-a-failure (the slice didn't exercise the\n      file; coverage didn't drop). Only exit 2 (real <100%) gates. Applies to smart-test:956 and both\n      ci.yml twins (911, 1156).\n  1d. [OPTIONAL, large speedup — owner decision] Narrow TEST SELECTION to merge-base too, restoring\n      ADR-0010's intended \"affected tests only\". Measured pathology: current per-PR runs ~the whole\n      suite (459 selected vs 436 total test files; 16338/16342 tests; 15.5 min @ 6 cores) because the\n      50-commit marker inflates the changed set to 113 files. Safe given step-3 teeth + nightly.\n  1e. Stream split (problem #2). The pass/fail summary + \"All changed source files at 100%\" verdict\n      print to smart-test STDOUT; .ci/pytest-output.log receives only raw pytest output — so the\n      file the handoff/ADR tell you to read never contains the green signal. Fix: also write the\n      scoped verdict into .ci/pytest-output.log (or a clearly-named companion).\n  TDD: add tests reproducing (green + 100% changed files -> exit 0) and (no-data changed file ->\n  not-fail), plus a unit for the branch-own changed-file computation.\n\nSTEP 2 — failover-aware full-suite marker/status write path (PRECONDITION for teeth; PR \"B\")\n  Make full-suite.yml write the last-green marker + aggregate commit status to the AUTHORITATIVE\n  remote (selfh under failover), mirroring the failover detection already in get_baseline and\n  auto-pr. Fixes the stale marker AND restores stop-the-line signaling under failover. Without this,\n  step-3 teeth would fail the full-suite JOB but the failure would not propagate to the (codeberg-\n  read) stop-the-line gate.\n\nSTEP 3 — full-suite coverage teeth (now safe AND effective; same PR \"B\")\n  Add `--cov-fail-under=100` to each full-suite per-package pytest; fix the `| tee` pipefail masking\n  so a coverage regression fails the job (full-suite already `exit 1`s on conclusion!=success at\n  1071-1081). Safe: no current whole-codebase debt (§3). Closes the cross-cutting-coverage crack in\n  the blocking path; cross-cutting regressions become attributable within ~12h + stop-the-line\n  instead of resting on nightly.\n\nSTEP 4 — incidental fixes (fold into PR \"C\" or wherever they touch)\n  - check-package-coverage: add \"rust-analyzer\" to default TARGETS (line 50) and accepted args (line\n    43). The PACKAGES map (line 31) already has it, but arg-parsing/defaults drop it, so the local\n    parity tool never checks 1 of the 6 marker-required packages.\n  - get_baseline (smart-test:251-257): correct the stale WI-tolil comment. It claims the marker is\n    \"inert today\"; the marker exists on selfh/badges and IS used (it is what anchors the 50-commit\n    baseline that drives BOTH the false-reds and the ~whole-suite per-PR runs).\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n5. WALL-CLOCK (measured / labeled extrapolation)\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  - Steps 2, 3, and 1a/1b/1c/1e: ~0 execution delta everywhere (checks/threshold on already-collected\n    data; failover-aware writes are metadata ops). Full-suite teeth change only the VERDICT, not the\n    work.\n  - Step 1d (narrow test selection): on-box (6 cores, -n auto) 15.5 min -> ~1-4 min typical; selfh\n    (-n 2, cgroup-capped) the same 459-file run extrapolates to ~40-50 min -> a few min (biggest\n    win); codeberg dormant under failover, same relative speedup when it resumes. No venue gets\n    slower (branch-own set ⊆ current set).\n  - Only real cost = teeth's stop-the-line exposure, de-risked by §3 (no debt) and gated behind\n    step 2.\n\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n6. GOVERNANCE / SCOPE\n════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  - scripts/smart-test, .github/workflows/**, scripts/check-package-coverage are NOT governance files\n    -> normal PR (no human-approval gate). ADR-0011 is edited in place (git history is the record).\n  - Suggested split: PR A = step 1 (smart-test correctness); PR B = steps 2+3 (failover-write +\n    teeth); PR C = step 4 (small fixes). Each independently testable; TDD; 100% coverage.\n  - OWNER DECISION: adopt step 1d (narrow TEST SELECTION to merge-base) now, or keep test selection\n    broad and fix only ENFORCEMENT scope (1a)? 1d is the large speedup but changes ADR-0010/0011\n    test-selection semantics; 1a alone removes the false-reds with ~0 wall-clock change.\n  - ADR touch: this updates ADR-0011's coverage-enforcement model (de-conflate test-selection\n    baseline from coverage-enforcement baseline; document that whole-codebase coverage is enforced by\n    full-suite teeth, not by the per-PR scoped gate). Update ADR-0011 in the same PR as step 1/3."  # d5dd
- op: discuss  # 2278
  at: '2026-07-11T23:30:43Z'  # 2278
  by: agent  # 2278
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2278
  clock: 3  # 2278
  nonce: '2278'  # 2278
  message: "IMPLEMENTED (2026-07-11) — 3 PRs merged on selfh/dev. The design comment above is the plan; this is the outcome.\n\nLANDED:\n- PR 1 (dev 606f0d6fa4) — smart-test correctness. get_baseline now returns\n  merge-base(HEAD, authoritative-dev) instead of the stale last-green marker\n  (Step 1a/1d); scoped gate distinguishes coverage.py \"No data to report\" from a\n  real <100% (Step 1c); pass/fail re-derivation word-bounds `[0-9]+ failed` so it\n  no longer matches \"N xfailed\" (Step 1b); scoped verdict written into\n  .ci/pytest-output.log (Step 1e). ADR-0011 updated (baseline decision reversal).\n- PR 2 (dev 5632bd6e73) — full-suite whole-codebase coverage teeth (Step 3): each\n  per-package job now fails unless its coverage is exactly 100%, reusing the same\n  `[ \"$COV\" = \"100\" ]` bar the last-green-marker write already applied. Plus the\n  ci.yml scoped-gate no-data distinction (Step 1c parity, both gate twins).\n- PR 3 (dev 101a49d084) — check-package-coverage now checks all six packages\n  (Step 4): rust-analyzer added to the default TARGETS + arg parser (it was in the\n  PACKAGES map but unreachable).\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE:\n- Branch-own baseline confirmed live: on PR 1's branch, `smart-test --manifest`\n  reported Baseline = 8dc4100e5f (merge-base), Changed files 6 (branch-own),\n  vs the pre-fix 113 files / 459-test (~whole-suite) manifest under the stale\n  038d4c4a marker. The drift files that WERE the dominant false-red source are\n  structurally absent from the changed set now.\n- 3-way scoped gate validated with controlled coverage data: 100% file -> PASS\n  (rc 0); no-data file -> WARN (not gating); <100% file -> FAIL (exit 1); a real\n  <100% file mixed with a 100% one still FAILs. Same validated for the ci.yml\n  gate twin.\n- Teeth validated end-to-end on a real package: rust-analyzer COV extracted = 100\n  -> teeth pass (exit 0); simulated COV=96 -> job fails (correct).\n- check-package-coverage rust-analyzer -> PASSED at 100% (arg now accepted; was\n  `Unknown argument`).\n- The false-red's premise (stale-marker drift) is removed structurally, and the\n  xfailed grep was proven a masked latent bug (PIPESTATUS default 0), not the\n  observed exit=1 — the exit=1 was the scoped gate (coverage.py exit 2 on\n  integration-covered drift / exit 1 \"No data\" conflated with <100%).\n\nHONEST RESIDUAL (No-Weasel): the DOMINANT, observed false-red (drift-driven) is\neliminated. A rare case can remain — a BRANCH-OWN file whose 100% coverage lives\noutside its reverse-dependency closure (integration-covered) could still read\npartial under the affected slice (Case D -> exit 2). That is a narrower and\narguably-legitimate \"this file isn't fully covered by its affected tests\" signal;\nthe whole-codebase backstop is now full-suite teeth (Step 3) + nightly. Not\naddressed further here.\n\nDEFERRED — Step 2 (failover-aware stop-the-line status endpoints). The option-b\ninvestigation refined the design's premise: the marker *push* already works (on\nthe selfh runner `origin` IS selfh, which is why selfh/badges is fresher than\ncodeberg/badges — the staleness is a flaky-job/all-100 artifact, now cosmetic\nsince PR 1 stopped using the marker as the baseline). The real failover gap is\nthat ci.yml's stop-the-line READ (ci.yml:106) and full-suite's status WRITE\n(full-suite:1052) both hardcode codeberg.org, so under failover the loop is\nconsistent-but-dead (writes/reads a down server -> stop-the-line effectively\ndisabled). Fix = point both at ${{ github.server_url }}/api/v1 (ci.yml:1178\nalready does this). NOT done here because it is (a) high-consequence — a wrong\nmove makes stop-the-line block ALL PRs — and (b) unvalidatable pre-merge\n(full-suite is schedule-only). Consequence of deferring: the teeth red full-suite\non a coverage regression (more signal than before) but do not yet BLOCK PRs under\nfailover; nightly still catches it. Pending explicit human go-ahead before\ntouching the stop-the-line endpoints.\n\nSTATUS: left open pending the Step-2 human decision. The core item complaint\n(false-red on green runs) is fixed; behavioral evidence above."  # 2278
