- op: discuss  # fcff
  at: '2026-07-12T00:34:15Z'  # fcff
  by: agent  # fcff
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fcff
  clock: 5  # fcff
  nonce: fcff  # fcff
  message: "RESOLVED (done) — 5 PRs merged on selfh/dev. Behavioral closure evidence below (the item's own filed repro, re-run, now exits 0).\n\nCORRECTED ROOT CAUSE — there were TWO distinct false-red mechanisms; the design comment above (and my first analysis) attributed the observed exit=1 to the coverage gate, which was only half right:\n\n  (A) DEV-LOOP symptom (what THIS item's repro actually hit in this shell).\n      This dev environment exports FORCE_COLOR=3, so pytest colorizes even the\n      redirected .ci/pytest-output.log. The summary line then begins with an ANSI\n      escape, so summarize_pytest_output's anchored `^=+ …` result-line grep fails\n      to match and — unguarded, under `set -e + pipefail` — ABORTS smart-test with\n      exit 1 AFTER the tests pass but BEFORE the coverage gate, on EVERY run\n      regardless of outcome. This is the item's \"exit 1 on fully-green runs\" AND\n      its problem #2 (\"missing green signal in captured output — jumps from one\n      divider straight to the end\"). The coverage gate was never even reached in\n      this env. Fixed in PR 5 (e1067a400a): the captured pytest run neutralizes\n      FORCE_COLOR/COLORTERM (aligning local with CI, which has neither), and the\n      result-line grep is `|| true`-guarded as defense in depth. CI was never\n      affected (no FORCE_COLOR there).\n\n  (B) CI-PATH coverage-gate false-red (distinct; real in CI where FORCE_COLOR is\n      absent). The scoped gate enforced 100% on the stale-last-green-marker-\n      inflated changed set; the affected slice under-covers integration-covered\n      DRIFT files → coverage.py exit 2 on a green branch; and it conflated \"No data\n      to report\" (exit 1) with a real <100%. Fixed by the branch-own merge-base\n      baseline (drift removed from the changed set) + the no-data distinction.\n\nTHE FIVE PRs:\n  - 606f0d6fa4  smart-test baseline -> merge-base(HEAD, authoritative-dev); no-data\n                distinction; xfailed grep word-bounded; verdict -> pytest log; ADR-0011.\n  - 5632bd6e73  full-suite whole-codebase coverage teeth (fail per-package job unless\n                exactly 100%); ci.yml scoped-gate no-data parity.\n  - 101a49d084  check-package-coverage checks all six packages (rust-analyzer added).\n  - 2eb0fc69a8  failover-aware commit-status endpoints (ci.yml stop-the-line read +\n                full-suite/nightly writes -> github.server_url) so teeth can BLOCK\n                under failover.\n  - e1067a400a  FORCE_COLOR fix (A above) — the actual dev-loop symptom.\n\nCLOSURE REPRO (behavioral evidence; the item's filed repro, FORCE_COLOR=3 active,\ndev @ e1067a400a): a green 100%-covered source change (comment on confidence.py),\n`BASE_BRANCH=selfh/dev scripts/smart-test` -> exit 0 (was 1). Output shows\n`✅ ==== 10256 passed, 2 skipped, 4 xfailed … =====`, the coverage gate now RUNS\nand passes (`Checking 100% coverage …` -> `✅ All changed source files are at 100%\ncoverage`), the verdict is written into .ci/pytest-output.log, and the log has 0\nANSI. Supporting live evidence: branch-own manifest (baseline=merge-base, 1 source\nfile vs pre-fix 113/459); teeth end-to-end (COV=100 pass, simulated 96 fails);\nstop-the-line read-fix self-validated on PR #576 (CI / stop-the-line: success =\nALLOW, no spurious block); check-package-coverage rust-analyzer -> PASSED at 100%.\n\nHONEST RESIDUAL (No-Weasel): a rare CI-path case remains — a BRANCH-OWN file whose\n100% coverage lives outside its reverse-dependency closure (integration-covered)\ncould still read partial under the affected slice (Case D -> exit 2). That is a\nnarrower, arguably-legitimate \"not fully covered by affected tests\" signal;\nwhole-codebase coverage is now backstopped by the full-suite teeth + nightly. And\nstop-the-line remains inherently WEAK by design (full-suite is schedule-only +\nper-SHA status + fast-moving dev), so a teeth-driven block only fires when a PR's\nbase SHA exactly matches a failed scheduled full-suite — the endpoint fix points\nthe plumbing at the right server but does not make stop-the-line strong (that would\nneed a push-trigger / status-propagation redesign, out of scope).\n\nSTATUS: done. The core complaint (false-red exit 1 on green + missing green signal)\nis fixed with the behavioral evidence above."  # fcff
